            "title": "Grindr's two top shareholders scrap $3.46 billion take-private bid after board ends talks",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "(Reuters) -Grindr's two largest shareholders said on Wednesday that they had withdrawn their proposed $3.46 billion offer to \u200btake the dating app private, shortly after the company ended talks over \u200cfinancing concerns.  Ray Zage and James Lu, who together own more than 60% of Grindr's outstanding shares,\u200c had offered $18 per share last month, representing a 51% premium over the company's stock price at the time.  The two shareholders said they \u200chad received strong interest from lenders and investors to support the transaction but did not disclose their names.",
